1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:05,827
OneNMRD Interface controls NMR
relaxometry experiments and

2
00:00:05,827 --> 00:00:08,715
analyses their NMRD profiles.

3
00:00:08,865 --> 00:00:12,524
It works with conventional and
fast-field-cycling consoles,

4
00:00:12,524 --> 00:00:14,115
in your web browser.

5
00:00:14,265 --> 00:00:19,248
Everything in this tour comes from its
built-in simulator: no hardware is moved.

6
00:00:20,748 --> 00:00:24,455
One interface drives different
consoles and magnets.

7
00:00:24,605 --> 00:00:28,716
FFC4, the fast-field-cycling
relaxometer at IST,

8
00:00:28,716 --> 00:00:32,749
runs on a Magritek Kea
console with Prospa.

9
00:00:32,899 --> 00:00:36,548
The Resonance Systems
ultraRelax8 runs through uSpin32,

10
00:00:36,548 --> 00:00:40,216
with generated run scripts
and its exported scans.

11
00:00:40,366 --> 00:00:45,155
The simulator stands in for either
console, for training and testing.

12
00:00:46,655 --> 00:00:51,557
Each console is chosen at the top,
with its own settings and hardware.

13
00:00:51,707 --> 00:00:55,389
On the ultraRelax8, the
field-cycling device levels,

14
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:58,434
V1 and V2, come from
the field calibration,

15
00:00:58,434 --> 00:01:00,696
within the firmware limits.

16
00:01:02,196 --> 00:01:05,551
The sequences are field-cycling
and standard ones.

17
00:01:05,701 --> 00:01:07,632
Eight field-cycling sequences:

18
00:01:07,632 --> 00:01:11,043
polarised at high field or
starting from a low field,

19
00:01:11,043 --> 00:01:15,126
with inversion or saturation,
each also with a solid echo.

20
00:01:15,276 --> 00:01:20,032
Inversion recovery and saturation
recovery are the standard T1 sequences,

21
00:01:20,032 --> 00:01:22,663
at fixed field, on the ultraRelax8.

22
00:01:22,813 --> 00:01:27,162
RF tuning, and a Tune of any
sequence, come before the run.

23
00:01:28,662 --> 00:01:32,216
Each timing diagram is drawn from
the sequence's own pulse program,

24
00:01:32,216 --> 00:01:34,052
with the current parameters.

25
00:01:34,202 --> 00:01:36,072
It shows the field switching,

26
00:01:36,072 --> 00:01:38,265
the RF pulses and the acquisition;

27
00:01:38,265 --> 00:01:41,453
every segment opens the
parameter behind it.

28
00:01:41,603 --> 00:01:44,860
The plan lists temperature,
field, sequence,

29
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:49,651
scans and τ values for each
row, and estimates the run time.

30
00:01:49,801 --> 00:01:53,198
Settings records which
sequences the hardware has.

31
00:01:54,698 --> 00:01:58,603
Run plan starts the experiment,
one row after another.

32
00:01:58,753 --> 00:02:03,318
Live acquisition shows every scan
as it arrives, with its spectrum.

33
00:02:03,468 --> 00:02:09,689
M is taken in the Mz window, with its σ,
the noise, and the signal-to-noise ratio.

34
00:02:09,839 --> 00:02:12,937
The average gets quieter
as the scans add up.

35
00:02:13,087 --> 00:02:17,114
M(τ) of the current field
builds up, point by point.

36
00:02:17,264 --> 00:02:20,916
When a field is complete, it
is fitted at once, with one,

37
00:02:20,916 --> 00:02:24,021
two or three exponentials,
in milliseconds.

38
00:02:24,171 --> 00:02:26,319
Meanwhile, Results follows the run:

39
00:02:26,319 --> 00:02:30,843
each finished field can be looked
at while the next one is measured.

40
00:02:32,343 --> 00:02:35,126
The noise analysis is your choice.

41
00:02:35,276 --> 00:02:37,820
The phase treatment can
be phase independent,

42
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:39,177
two-phase or four-phase,

43
00:02:39,177 --> 00:02:42,127
with the noise from the
scatter between scans.

44
00:02:42,277 --> 00:02:46,399
The previous Prospa analysis
stays available, for comparison.

45
00:02:46,549 --> 00:02:51,487
A Gaussian filter can be previewed
on the last scan before it is saved:

46
00:02:51,487 --> 00:02:52,322
here 20 kHz,

47
00:02:52,322 --> 00:02:56,497
with the filtered and unfiltered
averages side by side.

48
00:02:56,647 --> 00:02:58,007
On the ultraRelax8,

49
00:02:58,007 --> 00:03:03,162
a short noise and health check is
compared with the machine's reference,

50
00:03:03,162 --> 00:03:06,089
value by value, and kept as a trend.

51
00:03:07,589 --> 00:03:10,689
The final analysis is OneFit Engine's.

52
00:03:10,839 --> 00:03:13,893
Fit in OFE fits every field with OFE-Go,

53
00:03:13,893 --> 00:03:17,483
with MINOS errors and
reduced chi-square: here,

54
00:03:17,483 --> 00:03:20,353
four fields in about two seconds.

55
00:03:20,503 --> 00:03:22,426
The T1 dispersion is plotted,

56
00:03:22,426 --> 00:03:26,424
together with the T1 that
Prospa wrote, for comparison.

57
00:03:26,574 --> 00:03:30,762
The models are full OFE
expressions, and can be edited.

58
00:03:32,262 --> 00:03:36,732
Open in OFE-GUI sends the
fit to a running OFE-GUI.

59
00:03:36,882 --> 00:03:40,350
It refits it and plots every
field, to change the model,

60
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:42,558
the bounds or the plots there.

61
00:03:44,058 --> 00:03:48,521
The Terminal pane is a real shell
on the computer running OneNMRD,

62
00:03:48,521 --> 00:03:51,441
inside the page. It is off by default.

63
00:03:51,591 --> 00:03:56,071
Its Claude and Codex buttons start a
separately installed coding agent there,

64
00:03:56,071 --> 00:03:58,865
in a Docker sandbox when one is available.

65
00:03:59,015 --> 00:04:03,200
OneNMRD writes an AGENTS file
for them: how to reach the GUI,

66
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:06,089
the hardware rules, and the JSON API.

67
00:04:06,239 --> 00:04:10,265
Here the API lists the
run and its four fields.

68
00:04:10,415 --> 00:04:13,999
A Tune or a Run asked for by an
agent waits for your Approve;

69
00:04:13,999 --> 00:04:15,700
Stop is always allowed.

70
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:20,929
Plan, acquire, watch, and fit.

71
00:04:21,079 --> 00:04:25,310
OneNMRD Interface drives
FFC4 and the ultraRelax8,

72
00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:29,044
and hands the analysis to OneFit Engine.

73
00:04:29,194 --> 00:04:33,634
It is distributed under the
Artistic License 2.0. Prospa and

74
00:04:33,634 --> 00:04:35,854
uSpin32 are separate products,

75
00:04:35,854 --> 00:04:37,758
and are not included.
